<title>GERMANY: Lehnkering says 95/96 sales, profit up.</title>
<headline>Lehnkering says 95/96 sales, profit up.</headline>
<dateline>DUISBURG, Germany 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 1995/96 business year to September 30.</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Third-party sales			 922	vs 867.9</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		    30.5     vs 29.8</p>
<p>    Group net profit			  15.9     vs 14.5</p>
<p>    Group dividend recommendation	 9 marks  vs 9 marks</p>
<p>    Bonus					 1 mark   vs zero</p>
<p>    Group cash flow			   51.1     vs 49.8</p>
<p>    Group investment			  58.9     vs 36.1</p>
<p>    Group equity				131.8    vs 132.2</p>
<p>    Group workforce			   2,558    vs 2,045</p>
<p>    Group personnel costs		   185.7    vs 166.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German transport company, which is a unit of Preussag AG, is Lehnkehring Montan Transport AG.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
